# Single source of truth for the release this repo's `.github/workflows/release.yml` builds and
# publishes. Sourced (`. ./YMIR_VERSION`) by that workflow, and passed straight through to
# `Dockerfile` as build-args. Nothing here is bumped automatically - update it by hand, copying
# from ymir/bootstrap/YMIR_VERSION in a local checkout of github.com/GNU-Ymir/bootstrap, before
# dispatching a release. gymir and bootstrap are released in lockstep (same tag on both repos),
# so this file's values should always agree with whatever bootstrap/YMIR_VERSION says at the
# GYC_VERSION tag below - that's the "bootstrap is the value of truth" contract: this file only
# ever restates it, never invents a version of its own.
#
# - GYC_VERSION: the version this release is published under - the tag created on this repo
#   (github.com/GNU-Ymir/gymir) - and the matching git tag that must already exist on
#   github.com/GNU-Ymir/bootstrap, checked out during the build to get the self-hosted ymirc
#   source that gets compiled into ymir1 (see Make-lang.in's `ymir/libymirc.a` target, which
#   runs `gyllir build --release` against exactly that checkout). The release workflow fails
#   fast if that tag doesn't exist on bootstrap yet.
# - YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION / GCC_VERSION: the prebuilt `gyc` release this build's own ymirc
#   source is *compiled with* (not the version being built) - the same fact bootstrap/
#   YMIR_VERSION records from the bootstrap repo's point of view. Published as a .deb by
#   github.com/GNU-Ymir/gymir (release tag = YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION, asset =
#   gyc-<GCC major>_<YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION>_amd64.deb - only the GCC *major* appears in the
#   asset name).
# - GYLLIR_VERSION: the `gyllir` build tool release installed alongside it - it's what actually
#   invokes gyc to build ymir/bootstrap/libymirc.a during `make` (see Make-lang.in). Published
#   by github.com/GNU-Ymir/Gyllir (release tag = GYLLIR_VERSION, asset =
#   gyllir_<GYLLIR_VERSION>_amd64.deb).
# - MIDGARD_BRANCH: the github.com/GNU-Ymir/yruntime branch whose head is the standard library
#   (midgard) bundled into the produced gyc .deb - a branch, not a release tag. A yruntime release
#   is built with the gyc that bundles it, so it can only be tagged once that gyc is out; pinning a
#   tag here would ask for it before. That branch must declare (gyllir.toml) a version not tagged
#   yet, name GYC_VERSION as YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION in its own YMIR_VERSION, and - unless it is the
#   default branch - have an open pull request (see .github/scripts/midgard-branch.sh).
#   release.yml marks its head with the tag temp/<version> while it builds, then dispatches
#   yruntime's release on it, which tags <version> for real and merges that pull request.
# - YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_MIDGARD_VERSION: the midgard the ymirc source at GYC_VERSION is *compiled
#   against* - the std bootstrap's gyllir.toml/gyllir.lock pin, which gyllir stages under the
#   -iprefix the binding is compiled with. ymir1 links that midgard's runtime
#   (-lgymidgard-debug_<major.minor>, see Make-lang.in's YMIR_RUNTIME_LIBS), so it must be
#   installed on the build machine next to YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION's gyc. Not to be confused with
#   the midgard the gyc being built *ships*, which only exists once this release does.
GYC_VERSION=1.7.0
YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION=1.6.0
YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_MIDGARD_VERSION=1.9.0
GCC_VERSION=15.3.1
GYLLIR_VERSION=1.8.0
MIDGARD_BRANCH=MID-87-compile-from-1.7
